
assignment: Make a structural time series model and predict primary production based on the model

make an Rmd file with precise scientific description of all the steps in the methodology in markdown text and code in code blocks. Make a separate .R file for all functions. 

input: 
- pp_wide.csv, all measured parameters, including calculated integrated primary production (see below) 
- knmi_daily.csv (with daily irradiance)

Parameters have the following units and constraints
   parameter           unit                                        
 1 chlfa               ug/l                                        0 - 40
 2 turbidity           NTU                                         > 0
 3 O2                  mg/l                                        0 - 15
 4 perc_O2             %                                           0 - 100
 5 salinity            PSU                                         0 - 35
 6 PP_depth_integrated mg C/m2/d                                   > 0
 7 PBmax_EP            mgC (mg chla)-1 h-1                         > 0
 8 alfaB_EP            mgC (mg chla)-1 h-1)/(µmol fotonen m-2 s-1) > 0
 9 Eopt_EP             µmol fotonen m-2 s-1                        > 0
10 pH                  pH_units                                    > 0
11 irradiance_J_cm2    J/cm2                                       > 0
12 bottomdepth         m                                           > 0
13 Kd                  /m                                          > 0
14 conversionEtoC      molC/(mol fotons)                           > 0

do

- calculate incident PAR from irradiance

make functions 
- "fit_model"
- "make_predictions"

use R tidyverse and tidymodel workflows

fit parameters:
- PBmax (>0)
- alpha (>0)
- Eopt (>0)
- Kd (>0)
- Chl_surface (chlorophyll a in ug/l) (>0)

Test the distribution of all parameters. Remove outliers (based on all compartments per parameter), perpare for transformations if needed based on the distributions. 

prepare and run the model "long-term, seasonal and springbloom model" (LSS, output in "output_lss")

it includes:
- seasonal pattern with maximum during summer (all fit parameters except Kd)
- seasonal pattern with minimum during summer (Kd)
- long term linear term (all fit parameters)
- method to include the spring bloom dynamics (depending on compartment, usually a short burst of chlfa around March - May each year) this only applies to PBmax, alpha, and Chl_surface

Make models per compartiment

use fitted parameters to calculate daily primary production using an Eilers Peters model with photoinhibition using
- fitparameters Pmax, alpha and Eopt
- Chlorophyll-a
- Kd
- irradiance (for each day)

Visualize the contribution per model component (linear, season, spring bloom). Use an appropriate method

for each model save data and plots of:
- time series depth integrated daily modelled pp and daily observed pp (in dataset as PP_depth_integrated)
- XY diagrams of modelled vs observed vertically integrated production
- time series of all parameter estimates
- diagnostics
- observed vs predicted and residuals plot for all parameters

Prepare method to include additional measurments for chlfa and Kd (from MWTL)

Test all code with real data. 

